{"resourceIdentifier":"2884","resourceName":"Gansu Zhangye Grouped Afforestation Project","description":"Gansu Zhangye Grouped Afforestation Project (hereafter “the project”) is located in Zhangye City, Gansu Province of China. The project’s aim is to increase carbon sequestration and contribute to local sustainable development by planting trees on the barren lands. The grouped project combines multiple project activity instances into a single, combined project that adds new instances over time. The project proponent sets the geographic boundaries for the grouped project, including where new project activity instances may be added (Section 2.1.7), and establishes criteria for determining the eligibility of future instances (Section 2.1.21).\r\nFor the initial project activity instance, 11,011.93 ha of forest is to be planted by direct planting on barren lands in Zhangye City, and the planted trees and shrub are all native species which including Elaeagnus angustifolia (oleaster), Armeniaca sibirica (prumus armeniaca), Populus L. (aspen), Ulmus pumila L. (elm), Picea asperata Mast. (spruce), Pinus sylvestris (mongolian pine), Haloxylon ammodendron (synonym), Caragana korshinskii Kom (caragana microphylla) . It is expected that the scope of the project will increase. For the inclusion of new eligible areas as project instances willing to participate within the grouped project, the new areas shall meet the criteria listing in Section 2.1.21. According to the project design report, 53,000 hectares of new afforestation area is expected to be added from 2021 to 2027. The implementation of the afforestation project will generate GHG emission removals and mitigate climate change; improve soil and water conservation and forest cover; enhance local biodiversity by increasing the connectivity of forests and bring income and job opportunities for local communities and residents.","location":{"latitude":39.316468,"longitude":100.131699},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicC